      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Let's check this one.\n\nA common slip is to choose 3 or 81-related values without asking for the exponent.\n\n3^4=81, so log₃81=4. The logarithm is the exponent, not the base or the final number.\n\nNow use the same idea with fresh values.",
