    "teach_2": {
      "id": "teach_2",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "An exponent can be negative too.\n\n2^−3 = 1/8\nso\nlog₂(1/8) = −3\n\nA logarithm can therefore have a negative value even though its argument is positive.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_2_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_2_step": {
      "id": "teach_2_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "The reciprocal is the clue.\n\n1/25 = 5^−2\n\nSo a log with base 5 and argument 1/25 must be −2. Negative exponents create reciprocals.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_2"
        }
      ]
    },
