    "teach_3": {
      "id": "teach_3",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "The base does not have to be a whole number.\n\n0.1 = 10^−1.\nSo 0.1^3 = 0.001, which means:\n\nlog₀.₁ 0.001 = 3.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_3_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_3_step": {
      "id": "teach_3_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "With decimal bases, powers of 10 make the pattern easy.\n\n0.01 = 10^−2\n0.000001 = 10^−6\n\nIf (10^−2)^x = 10^−6, then −2x=−6, so x=3.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_3"
        }
      ]
    },
