    "teach_5": {
      "id": "teach_5",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "A logarithm can hide the number instead of the exponent.\n\nlog₈ x = 2/3\nmeans\nx = 8^(2/3).\n\nCube root first: ∛8=2. Then square: 2^2=4.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_5_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_5_step": {
      "id": "teach_5_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "So log₈x=2/3 gives x=4.\n\nThis is the same definition again: log form tells you the exponent; exponential form gives you the number.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_5"
        }
      ]
    },
