    "teach_8": {
      "id": "teach_8",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "One final translation can combine a fractional and a negative exponent.\n\nlog₄ x = −3/2\nmeans\nx = 4^(−3/2).\n\n√4=2, 2^3=8, then the negative sign takes the reciprocal: x=1/8.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_8_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_8_step": {
      "id": "teach_8_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "A reliable order is:\n\n1. Use the denominator as a root.\n2. Use the numerator as a power.\n3. If the exponent is negative, take the reciprocal.\n\nThen check by raising the original base.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_8"
        }
      ]
    },
